Install the ze/ocl backend DLLs on Windows (missing RUNTIME install rule).

The rt-backend-cuda/hip/omp install rules declare RUNTIME, LIBRARY and
ARCHIVE destinations, but rt-backend-ze and rt-backend-ocl declare only
LIBRARY and ARCHIVE. On Windows a shared library's .dll is a RUNTIME
artifact, and CMake silently skips artifact kinds that have no install
rule — so both backends build fine but only their import .lib files are
installed; the .dll files never reach the install tree and the backends
cannot load at runtime. Add the same RUNTIME destination the other three
backends already use. No effect on Linux (a .so is a LIBRARY artifact).

diff --git a/src/runtime/CMakeLists.txt b/src/runtime/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/src/runtime/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/runtime/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -234,4 +234,5 @@
   install(TARGETS rt-backend-ze
+        RUNTIME DESTINATION bin/hipSYCL
         LIBRARY DESTINATION lib/hipSYCL
         ARCHIVE DESTINATION lib/hipSYCL)
 endif()
@@ -289,4 +290,5 @@
   install(TARGETS rt-backend-ocl
+        RUNTIME DESTINATION bin/hipSYCL
         LIBRARY DESTINATION lib/hipSYCL
         ARCHIVE DESTINATION lib/hipSYCL)
 endif()
